599 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 121 0 R
/T (5.1: Arduino IDE The Arduino Integrated Development Environment \(IDE\) is a cross-platform, open-source application used to write, compile, and upload sketches \(programs\) to Arduino microcontroller boards. Written in Java, the IDE provides a simple editor with syntax highlighting, a serial monitor, and a board/library manager. Version 2.x introduces a language server protocol \(LSP\) backend for autocompletion and on-the-fly error checking. In this project, the Arduino IDE is used to compile the servo control sketch and upload it to the Arduino UNO via USB. SOFTWARE USED)
/E (5.1: Arduino IDE The Arduino Integrated Development Environment \(IDE\) is a cross-platform, open-source application used to write, compile, and upload sketches \(programs\) to Arduino microcontroller boards. Written in Java, the IDE provides a simple editor with syntax highlighting, a serial monitor, and a board/library manager. Version 2.x introduces a language server protocol \(LSP\) backend for autocompletion and on-the-fly error checking. In this project, the Arduino IDE is used to compile the servo control sketch and upload it to the Arduino UNO via USB. SOFTWARE USED)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
